📅 Day 40 – DOM Manipulation in JavaScript

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on DOM (Document Object Model) Manipulation in JavaScript. The mentor explained how the DOM represents the structure of an HTML document and how JavaScript can dynamically access and modify elements.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Introduction to DOM
DOM represents the HTML document as a tree structure
Allows JavaScript to access and modify webpage elements
Enables dynamic updates without reloading the page

2️⃣ DOM Selection Methods
getElementById() → Select element by ID
getElementsByClassName() → Select elements by class
querySelector() → Select first matching element
querySelectorAll() → Select all matching elements

3️⃣ DOM Manipulation
Changing text content → innerText, innerHTML
Modifying styles → style.color, style.backgroundColor
Handling user interactions
Updating elements dynamically

🔹 Practical Work
Accessed HTML elements using DOM methods
Modified text and styles dynamically
Implemented user interaction using JavaScript
Observed real-time changes without page reload